  "ground_truth_protocol": {
    "protocol_name": "DNP3",
    "version": "IEEE 1815-2012",
    "description": "DNP3 over TCP/UDP 20000. The 10-byte link header is followed by 16-byte user-data blocks each closed by a CRC; the first block starts with the transport header and the application header whose function code selects the message type (link-only frames are typed by the link function). Derived from the Wireshark/tshark dissection of the benchmark capture (dol/truth-file-derivation/scripts/build_truth.py): fields at a fixed offset in at least 60% of a type's messages, bitfields sharing a byte merged, arrays of 3+ equal fields and variable-position content kept as one bytes field (the modbus.json convention for register arrays); types with fewer than 5 messages are omitted.",
    "offset_convention": "Link-header fields use wire-absolute offsets 0..9; the other types are relative to offset 10 (first data block). Offsets are wire offsets, i.e. the block CRCs are counted.",
